      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? These are some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg** per dose, at a different frequency\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
